# Methodology Page Structure

Under `web-foundations/docs/methodology/`, every content page is a **directory named by slug** containing `index.md`. Never add a bare `slug.md` next to language roots or sibling page folders.

## Required layout

```
methodology/
  en/
    index.md                                    ← language hub only
    ai-practical-guide/index.md
    ai-assisted-development-foundations/index.md  ← public manifesto; architecture primer is lessons/en/ai-assisted-development/foundations/
    tao-of-ai-development/index.md   ← permalink stub; full chapter in ~/src/ttod/sources/tao-of-ai-development/
  es/
    index.md
    ai-practical-guide/index.md
    ai-assisted-development-foundations/index.md  ← mismo manifiesto (ES)
    uso-ia-specs-arquitectura/index.md
    ai-practical-guide/tao-of-ai-development/index.md   ← stub; same TTOD home
```

## Rules when creating or renaming

1. **New page** → `mkdir methodology/{en|es}/<slug>` then write `<slug>/index.md`.
2. **Never** create `methodology/{en|es}/<slug>.md` at the language-root level.
3. **Front matter `permalink`** (when present) must end with a trailing slash matching the dir:
   `/methodology/{lang}/<slug>/`
4. **Cross-links** prefer directory URLs (`../other-slug/` or site permalinks), not `other-slug.md`.
5. Nested pages (e.g. Tao under the practical guide) still use `…/<slug>/index.md`.
6. If you find a legacy bare `.md` page, convert with:
   `mkdir -p <slug> && mv <slug>.md <slug>/index.md` and fix relative links one level deeper.

## Why

Jekyll pretty URLs, lesson navigation, and bilingual parity all assume slug folders. Bare files break permalink consistency and force brittle `.md` relative links.
